{:edb/db-before-t 2236 :edb/db-after-t 2237 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535549 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:22:07.349Z" 13194139535549 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354860 13194139535549 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354867 13194139535549 true] [17592186101458 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535549 true] [17592186101458 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535549 false] [17592186101458 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies $y(1)=2.$ Assume that $x>0.$" 13194139535549 true] [17592186101458 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies $y(1) = 2$. Assume that $x > 0$." 13194139535549 false] [17592186101458 1145 "For $x>0$ and the branch through $y(1)=2$, separate and integrate:\n$$\\frac{dy}{y^2}=\\frac{dx}{x},\\qquad -\\frac1y=\\ln x+C.$$\nThe initial condition gives $C=-1/2$, so\n$$y=\\frac2{1-2\\ln x}.$$\nThe maximal interval containing $x=1$ is $0<x<\\sqrt e$." 13194139535549 false] [17592186101458 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $x>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+C} & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{C} & =2 \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=2$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{-1}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2})}=\\frac{2}{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354860 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354861 13194139535549 true] [17592186354860 1089 "q-104058" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354860 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535549 true] [17592186354860 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354860 1113 #uuid "f1428f3d-5054-5866-8041-e9c9eed9b449" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354860 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|-1 & ={1}^{2}+C \\\\ 0-1 & =1+C \\\\ C & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2\\,.\n$$" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354862 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354863 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354864 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354865 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354866 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1041 "selection" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354865 13194139535549 true] [17592186354861 1110 #uuid "921db6b7-2b72-5413-ada5-2ba6ae2de3c2" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354862 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535549 true] [17592186354862 1111 #uuid "3499a528-3b5b-5342-a45f-58ae5606f8f8" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354863 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y=2{x}^{2}+2" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535549 true] [17592186354863 1111 #uuid "13e70303-6e01-5cc5-bb94-b26acfeeebfb" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354864 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y={x}^{2}+2" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535549 true] [17592186354864 1111 #uuid "b7b648b8-3bba-5404-bcfd-aefa9938d0b5" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354865 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535549 true] [17592186354865 1111 #uuid "6024ef2e-28f1-5f1a-b820-5f13c5c76835" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354866 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y=2{x}^{2}-2" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535549 true] [17592186354866 1111 #uuid "83146c73-c536-5451-b0e3-e6238f76276e" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354867 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354868 13194139535549 true] [17592186354867 1089 "q-8306" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354867 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535549 true] [17592186354867 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354867 1113 #uuid "177e97c5-b0fe-5fdf-abe1-80b42d3faf53" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354867 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}/3} & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{4/3} & =1 \\\\ K & ={e}^{-4/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4/3}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354869 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354870 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354871 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354872 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354873 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1041 "selection" 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354873 13194139535549 true] [17592186354868 1110 #uuid "4ddc